1
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:16,310
<i>Gadiel, thank you for your letter.</i>

2
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:18,460
<i>We've been apart, but how are you?</i>

3
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:23,920
<i>My family continues to force me to learn 
how to be a proper lady and stuff.</i>

4
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,550
<i>If you were here, 
I bet you'd say something like,</i>

5
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:31,610
<i>"Surely they're only thinking 
of what's best for you."</i>

6
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:36,320
<i>But I </i>know<i> it's just my father and everyone
in the mansion being mean to me.</i>

7
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:42,150
<i>Well, anyways, I'd be happy 
if you came to see me again.</i>

8
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:47,030
<i>Oh, yeah, and there seems to be 
a nasty cold going around,</i>

9
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:49,580
<i>so be careful, okay? Rafilia.</i>

10
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:25,060
THE HEALING PRINCESS

11
00:02:26,990 --> 00:02:30,170
You have a high fever. Please open your mouth.

12
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:34,840
<i>His tonsils are swollen too.</i>

13
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:37,980
<i>These are the symptoms of the cold
 that's been sweeping through.</i>

14
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:42,140
When did your son come down with the fever?

15
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:44,270
Huh? Let's see...

16
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:45,500
It was this morning.

17
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,770
It came on suddenly earlier today.

18
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:50,110
Was he coughing before that?

19
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:53,430
Now that you mention it... Yes, he was.

20
00:02:54,990 --> 00:02:57,700
It'd be best to give him something
for the fever immediately.

21
00:02:58,070 --> 00:03:00,580
It's not good to keep up one this high.

22
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:05,410
<i>He's sweating an awful lot, so I need
to make sure he's not dehydrated as well.</i>

23
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:08,830
Please take him to an isolated room.

24
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:10,700
Understood.

25
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,140
May I accompany him?

26
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:17,590
I'm afraid I can't allow that. 
You may catch his illness.

27
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:18,870
But...

28
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:22,310
Please rest assured. 
He'll get better within three days.

29
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:23,450
What about medicines?!

30
00:03:23,450 --> 00:03:26,560
I heard you have medicines
here that work really well.

31
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,480
The antipyretic and the cold medicine, please.

32
00:03:41,170 --> 00:03:42,530
Are these the ones?

33
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:44,700
Yes, thank you very much.

34
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:52,430
For a child, split each tablet
 into three equal doses

35
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:55,990
and have him take one twice 
a day at 12-hour intervals.

36
00:03:56,590 --> 00:03:58,640
Let's see how he does with that first.

37
00:03:58,990 --> 00:04:00,090
Very well.

38
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:03,480
After meals, have him take the cold medicine.

39
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,120
Understood.

40
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:07,870
Let's leave this to them.

41
00:04:07,870 --> 00:04:10,740
Okay. Please look after my boy.

42
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:12,690
We will.

43
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:17,900
You're both lucky to have the princess 
herself perform an examination.

44
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:20,330
U-Um, whoever do you mean?

45
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:22,370
I am not a princess!

46
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:28,790
She's widely known as the Healing Princess.

47
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:33,460
Hey, I've asked you to stop calling me that!

48
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,250
My apologies.

49
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:36,760
It's really embarrassing!

50
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:36,760
Ellen, it's time.

51
00:04:36,990 --> 00:04:38,550
Oh, right.

52
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:41,380
Well, I'll be taking my leave now.

53
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:44,260
Thank you for what you've done!

54
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:51,270
Um, were those people...

55
00:04:55,770 --> 00:04:59,110
So you're saying with the medicine 
from this "Healing Princess,"

56
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:00,610
he was cured in three days?

57
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:04,900
That's right! By the next day, 
my son's fever had already broken.

58
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:07,140
I was truly shocked.

59
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:11,930
At first, I thought she might be a wizard
who's made a pact with a spirit,

60
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:14,140
but she's apparently an apothecary of sorts.

61
00:05:14,670 --> 00:05:18,710
I guess the rumor that these medicines 
are blessed by the spirits is true.

62
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,680
And you believe the 
Vankreift family to be involved?

63
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:25,430
Yes. I believe the man 
with the girl was probably...

64
00:05:26,090 --> 00:05:28,360
the hero himself.

65
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:33,350
You're Hume the court healer, yes?

66
00:05:33,350 --> 00:05:35,060
Y-Yes, sire.

67
00:05:35,530 --> 00:05:37,520
I read your petition.

68
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:42,490
You wish to investigate the medicines
 of the Vankreift family.

69
00:05:42,810 --> 00:05:43,390
Yes, sire.

70
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:48,080
I, too, am curious about these medicines 
supposedly effective against the epidemic.

71
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,200
P-Please forgive me for speaking—

72
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,580
That's not necessary.

73
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:52,040
I've looked into things.

74
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:58,950
You want those medicines, don't you?

75
00:05:59,530 --> 00:06:03,920
For your mother,
 whose condition fails to improve.

76
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:08,100
P-Please do forgive me for speaking up.

77
00:06:09,190 --> 00:06:12,100
This again after I told you 
it wasn't necessary?

78
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:14,350
All right, I'll forgive you.

79
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:19,070
I can't deny that my petition
 had selfish motivation.

80
00:06:19,530 --> 00:06:24,380
But the merchants are all scrambling
 to get their hands on these medicines.

81
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:29,020
If we, the court healers, 
don't come up with them soon,

82
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,240
we risk losing the people's trust.

83
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,760
That was my thinking.

84
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,000
Oh?

85
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,750
Please, permit me to research these medicines!

86
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:42,170
The people's trust, hmm?

87
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,840
So be it.

88
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:49,980
Thank you very much, sire!

89
00:06:51,070 --> 00:06:56,230
I am allowing this primarily because 
you're a spirit wizard at such a young age.

90
00:06:58,170 --> 00:07:01,630
I just adore people with bright futures.

91
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:06,760
However, there are terms you must
 adhere to in your research, Hume.

92
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:12,190
The Vankreifts are very special 
to the royal family, after all.

93
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:18,780
You're free to go. I'll notify you later.

94
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:20,060
Yes, sire.

95
00:07:25,450 --> 00:07:26,950
Summon Gadiel.

96
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:28,010
Yes, sire!

97
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:36,180
<i>He seemed to be in a good mood, 
but something lurks behind that smile...</i>

98
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:41,240
<i>I can only assume it has 
to do with the Vankreift family.</i>

99
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:47,360
<i>Perhaps that is territory I best not tread.</i>

100
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:57,350
And? Are you still exchanging letters
 with Sauvel's daughter?

101
00:07:57,670 --> 00:08:01,100
Yes, although I only reply occasionally.

102
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,360
I see.

103
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:07,550
It would appear the Vankreift family
 has recently hired a skilled apothecary.

104
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,760
An apothecary?

105
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:15,520
They say it was none other than 
the spirit princess herself who hired them.

106
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,760
Huh? Ellen did?

107
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:24,930
The number of people staying in our lands
for medical purposes has increased

108
00:08:24,930 --> 00:08:26,830
about 30 percent since last month.

109
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:29,070
Thirty percent is a lot.

110
00:08:29,070 --> 00:08:32,780
Consequently, we haven't been able
 to keep our medical stores supplied.

111
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:38,280
Those in urgent need are even starting
 to argue over medicine.

112
00:08:40,070 --> 00:08:42,460
We may need to begin triage.

113
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:45,110
Triage?

114
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:49,420
The practice of prioritizing patients
based on the severity of their condition.

115
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:55,680
Children, pregnant women, and the unconscious,
who are more susceptible, will be put first.

116
00:08:56,050 --> 00:08:57,520
The same goes for injuries.

117
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,630
Yes, that's a good plan.

118
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:03,890
Leave it to Lady Ellen to come up 
with one so quickly.

119
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:06,430
Pawpaw is very impressed!

120
00:09:06,430 --> 00:09:08,530
You've been a tremendous help, Ellen.

121
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:11,560
I'm sorry to always be relying on you.

122
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:16,380
I mean, my knowledge comes 
from my ancestors.

123
00:09:16,710 --> 00:09:19,000
It's not like I came up with it myself.

124
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:23,550
To be praised so enthusiastically always 
makes me feel a bit guilty.

125
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:28,840
You take your ancestors' knowledge 
and apply that where it's needed.

126
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:33,080
Wherever they are now, 
I'm sure they're resting in peace.

127
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:35,480
Yes, you're right.

128
00:09:38,110 --> 00:09:41,390
Ah, my daughter's just the best!

129
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:44,100
Father, you're annoying!

130
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:46,190
Brother, you fawn on her too much.

131
00:09:46,470 --> 00:09:49,420
Huh?! I don't want to hear 
that from the likes of you, Sauvel!

132
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:52,440
You don't care enough
 about your own daughter!

133
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:02,290
Rafilia, are you awake?

134
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:14,340
My daughter is in her rebellious phase.

135
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:17,050
You don't think she's sulking 
because you ignore her?

136
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,280
That may be the truth of it.

137
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:26,390
Brother, to get us back to the topic at hand,
 we have a problem to discuss.

138
00:10:26,390 --> 00:10:27,220
Hmm?

139
00:10:27,530 --> 00:10:31,540
Perhaps due to the increase in people 
staying here for medical reasons,

140
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:35,190
I've recently received reports 
about deteriorations in public safety.

141
00:10:39,950 --> 00:10:42,410
Huh? What is it?

142
00:10:42,730 --> 00:10:47,240
Ellen may be smart, but she's truly clueless 
when it comes to matters concerning herself.

143
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,430
There's nothing you can do about that.

144
00:10:50,430 --> 00:10:54,470
Not even Ellen could be 
so self-aware at her age.

145
00:10:54,470 --> 00:10:56,180
Yeah, that's true.

146
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:57,380
Roren.

147
00:10:59,570 --> 00:11:00,840
Understood.

148
00:11:02,010 --> 00:11:04,370
I see. You're going to summon <i>him</i>, huh?

149
00:11:04,370 --> 00:11:06,470
We've spoken on this before, haven't we?

150
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:08,110
Do you still not trust him?

151
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:11,820
What is this all about?

152
00:11:12,170 --> 00:11:15,030
Well, you see, the rumors are already
 spreading through the land

153
00:11:15,810 --> 00:11:20,440
that the young lady from the Vankreift
 family is the one administering medicines.

154
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:24,200
If things continue the way they are, 
your life may be in danger, Ellen.

155
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:29,420
So in other words, 
this person you've sent for is...

156
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,440
He's your bodyguard, Ellen.

157
00:11:32,510 --> 00:11:34,290
I've brought them, Your Grace.

158
00:11:34,290 --> 00:11:34,880
Come in.

159
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,760
Please meet my son.

160
00:11:43,390 --> 00:11:44,980
<i>Your</i> son, Uncle Alberto?

161
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:48,840
I believe Kai turns thirteen this year.

162
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:51,690
I didn't know you were married, Uncle!

163
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:54,550
Do I look a bachelor to you?

164
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:59,230
More like... you're always so busy working
that I never sensed a woman in your life.

165
00:11:59,230 --> 00:12:02,910
While I'm working... 
Yes, I suppose you're right there.

166
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:06,120
Nice to meet you. My name is Kai.

167
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:12,290
Nice to meet you as well. My name is Ellen.

168
00:12:13,550 --> 00:12:16,590
Lady Ellen, my father told me everything.

169
00:12:16,930 --> 00:12:20,980
Truly, thank you so much 
for saving him when you did.

170
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:25,470
I shall do my best to protect you.

171
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:28,870
Oh, no, I didn't...

172
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:31,850
Yes, well, someone here doesn't approve of this.

173
00:12:31,850 --> 00:12:32,440
Huh?

174
00:12:32,990 --> 00:12:36,400
Specifically, the problem lies 
with using a human bodyguard.

175
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,110
What do you mean?

176
00:12:38,570 --> 00:12:41,240
Hey. You can hear us, can't you?

177
00:12:47,450 --> 00:12:49,210
Huh?! Brother...

178
00:12:49,210 --> 00:12:52,170
It's all right. Van, introduce yourself.

179
00:12:52,770 --> 00:12:56,920
I am Van, child of the Great Wind Spirit Vint.

180
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:58,130
Lady Ellen, watch out—

181
00:12:58,350 --> 00:12:59,840
Fluffy!

182
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:03,600
It's all right! Van is a good boy.

183
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:06,310
You smell so nice!

184
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,020
I just had a bath.

185
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:11,350
Hmph, kid.

186
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:14,650
You say you're going to protect the princess? 
Don't make me laugh.

187
00:13:14,970 --> 00:13:15,900
What was that?!

188
00:13:19,530 --> 00:13:23,410
In conclusion, Ellen is going to have
 a guard from the spirit world as well.

189
00:13:24,250 --> 00:13:26,550
Van can freely manipulate wind,

190
00:13:26,550 --> 00:13:31,060
and his hearing is so sharp that he 
can even pick up rumors from afar.

191
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,480
He'll prove useful.

192
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:34,630
Y-Yes, but still, Brother...

193
00:13:34,630 --> 00:13:38,340
A beast of this size will cause 
a commotion in town.

194
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:39,710
Not a problem.

195
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:45,220
Princess, what do you think?

196
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:50,620
Van, you learned to humanize! 
It's great! You look so handsome!

197
00:13:51,070 --> 00:13:55,150
Of course I do! I <i>am</i> handsome,
 not to mention amazing!

198
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:01,850
What's wrong, kid?

199
00:14:01,850 --> 00:14:03,150
You're not better than me!

200
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:09,120
Hey, you guys! What are you 
fighting over Ellen for?!

201
00:14:09,370 --> 00:14:13,330
This just won't do! I'll protect Ellen myself!

202
00:14:13,330 --> 00:14:15,580
I'm not letting either of you
 marry my daughter!

203
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:18,430
Brother?

204
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:21,420
Father, you're annoying.

205
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:30,400
Hume, let's find a close inn for the night.

206
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,850
Could you please keep your distance?

207
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:36,560
Hume! How could you speak 
to the prince in that manner?!

208
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:41,570
I don't have a choice.
 My spirit is terrified of him.

209
00:14:42,430 --> 00:14:44,870
It's all right, Vogel. It's the truth.

210
00:14:45,750 --> 00:14:49,580
And I'm not the prince right now. 
Call me Gaddis.

211
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:52,700
There's no telling when
someone might be listening.

212
00:14:53,170 --> 00:14:54,790
My apologies.

213
00:14:55,230 --> 00:15:00,590
We have to get a hold of those medicines
and figure out how they're produced.

214
00:15:01,350 --> 00:15:04,510
We have to find out how this young 
Vankreift lady is involved,

215
00:15:04,850 --> 00:15:07,220
and whether spirits are the ones making them.

216
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:10,260
My spirit will be the one running 
that investigation.

217
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:13,660
What will you do if my spirit
 is too afraid to work?

218
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:17,080
It's precisely as he says.

219
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:20,170
Still, it doesn't fully make sense to me.

220
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:21,110
What doesn't?

221
00:15:21,450 --> 00:15:24,300
What is His Majesty thinking?

222
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:27,380
Why is he making our prince
 do this kind of work?

223
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:30,230
Rabe, how many times must I tell you?

224
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:31,240
I'm Gaddis.

225
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:34,120
Oh, my apologies.

226
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:36,900
Either way, this is incredible.

227
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:40,040
How the wind spirits are blowing

228
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:44,300
the disease up into the sky to prevent its 
spread, purifying it in the process.

229
00:15:46,630 --> 00:15:48,220
What power...

230
00:15:56,420 --> 00:15:58,670
My spirit is getting frightened.

231
00:15:59,410 --> 00:16:02,440
I've no doubt there's a 
high-ranking wind spirit here.

232
00:16:03,090 --> 00:16:08,180
The rumors of a spirit making the 
medicines might actually be true.

233
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:08,990
Wait!

234
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:13,480
<i>Could it be that Ellen is 
the one making the medicine?</i>

235
00:16:14,490 --> 00:16:16,580
Your H— Gaddis?

236
00:16:17,030 --> 00:16:17,910
Yeah.

237
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:21,920
<i>I know I'm being selfish.</i>

238
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:27,260
<i>Still, my desire to see you hasn't changed.</i>

239
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:35,720
Lady Rafilia.

240
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:39,310
A letter addressed to you, milady.

241
00:16:40,910 --> 00:16:42,060
Thank you!

242
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:45,070
It's from Gadiel!

243
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:48,030
Milady, you musn't use 
the prince's name so casually!

244
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,240
Oh, shut up! You can leave already!

245
00:16:58,150 --> 00:17:01,190
What's this? No way!

246
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:03,220
Oh, Gadiel...

247
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:12,220
By the way, what's Uncle Alberto's wife like?

248
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:15,670
She's quite brave and very reliable.

249
00:17:16,090 --> 00:17:20,850
Um, it's a little embarrassing to hear 
you describe my mother that way.

250
00:17:21,930 --> 00:17:25,820
It sounds like your mother 
is the one holding the crop.

251
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:28,040
Oh, yes, most def—

252
00:17:29,310 --> 00:17:30,490
That's what I thought!

253
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:34,820
But I suppose that suits 
Uncle Alberto perfectly.

254
00:17:36,910 --> 00:17:39,790
Next time, I'll introduce you
 to her, Lady Ellen.

255
00:17:39,790 --> 00:17:41,620
Really?! I can't wait to meet her!

256
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:44,580
By all means, please visit our home!

257
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:46,540
Did he just invite her over?

258
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,300
Meeting his mother?

259
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:49,820
I won't stand for it!

260
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:51,670
Father, you're being loud.

261
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:52,510
Meanie!

262
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:55,720
Brother, I see Ellen holds <i>your</i> crop.

263
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:59,050
Of course! If it's Ellen, I don't 
mind getting my butt whipped!

264
00:17:59,050 --> 00:18:01,280
Mother is going to be upset.

265
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:07,350
I'm just kidding, Ori!
 I'd only let you whip me, Ori!

266
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:13,060
Princess!

267
00:18:14,310 --> 00:18:16,360
I'm going to go take a look around.

268
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:18,950
If you need anything, just call on me.

269
00:18:18,950 --> 00:18:22,000
Okay. You be careful too, Van.

270
00:18:25,130 --> 00:18:28,430
About the triage proposal you suggested...

271
00:18:28,430 --> 00:18:31,210
It was going well amongst the healers,

272
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:37,800
but there are countless patients 
insisting they were here first.

273
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:43,770
Everyone seems anxious about whether
 or not they'll get medicine.

274
00:18:43,770 --> 00:18:47,370
Then I'll just make more 
so that everyone can—

275
00:18:47,370 --> 00:18:48,320
Ellen.

276
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:51,150
I understand how you feel, 
but the answer is no.

277
00:18:51,470 --> 00:18:55,120
We talked at length about limits
 on what you can make, didn't we?

278
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:59,950
But I want to ease everyone's concerns.

279
00:19:00,730 --> 00:19:02,700
Father, just a little...

280
00:19:03,110 --> 00:19:06,430
Can I please make just a little bit more?

281
00:19:15,090 --> 00:19:16,080
Ellen.

282
00:19:18,310 --> 00:19:20,470
Please take care not to push yourself.

283
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:25,080
Yes, sir. I understand.

284
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:36,550
What?

285
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:37,700
A tiger?!

286
00:19:38,910 --> 00:19:41,980
Wait! Sorry for startling everyone!

287
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:43,800
He's a spirit!

288
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:51,340
I am the princess's bodyguard, Van.

289
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:53,210
Oh...

290
00:19:53,210 --> 00:19:54,920
Welcome home!

291
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:57,130
Pawpaw! I'm back!

292
00:19:57,130 --> 00:20:00,090
Hello, Lady Ellen!

293
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:05,270
I'll prepare some special 
tea just for you, Lady Ellen!

294
00:20:06,430 --> 00:20:06,890
Roren!

295
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:07,910
Yes?

296
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:11,200
I plan to have dinner 
with Rafilia and Aria tonight.

297
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,770
Please let them know.

298
00:20:12,770 --> 00:20:16,360
How delightful. As you wish, Your Grace.

299
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:18,070
Include Mother as well.

300
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:20,820
Of course, Your Grace.

301
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:29,210
I did as you suggested, Lady Ellen, 
and the vegetables have grown well.

302
00:20:29,210 --> 00:20:31,270
I'm so glad!

303
00:20:31,270 --> 00:20:34,810
Now that you mention it, I heard 
from Uncle that you wanted

304
00:20:34,810 --> 00:20:36,880
some advice on the fertilizer for the fields.

305
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:39,530
I would love to see them firsthand,

306
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:42,590
so once things are settled with the
treatment center, let's go together.

307
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:44,360
That would be helpful.

308
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:46,630
Come in.

309
00:20:48,770 --> 00:20:51,150
Your Grace, Lady Rafilia
 is nowhere to be found.

310
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:52,360
What?

311
00:20:52,610 --> 00:20:55,720
I've searched the whole mansion 
and she's nowhere to be found.

312
00:21:00,330 --> 00:21:00,950
Rafilia!

313
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:12,000
Aria!

314
00:21:13,570 --> 00:21:15,750
Aria, do you know where Rafilia is?

315
00:21:18,890 --> 00:21:19,990
I see.

316
00:21:21,190 --> 00:21:23,180
Is something the matter with her?

317
00:21:24,650 --> 00:21:27,660
Rafilia is missing.

318
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:28,640
What?

319
00:21:32,510 --> 00:21:36,020
This is because I didn't take 
the time to listen to her.

320
00:21:37,290 --> 00:21:39,490
Could she have... run away from home?

321
00:21:48,190 --> 00:21:49,620
Van?

322
00:21:55,330 --> 00:22:03,910
"Must get medicine... from the Vankreift 
family... we must... the young lady."

323
00:22:06,730 --> 00:22:08,640
I heard a voice saying that.

324
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:09,850
What did you say?!

325
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:12,310
Could it be...

326
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:19,230
Was she mistakenly kidnapped instead of me?

327
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:24,630
Translation: Yukari Murase-Louden

328
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:28,340
Editing: Riley Dalton

329
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:31,850
Quality Check: Ashley Barboza
Translation Check: Elizabeth Ellis

